This copies `draft[draft.activeTab].pendingInput` (and all other mirrored fields) into the flat state. The function definition (lines 87–101):

```typescript
/** Copy all mirrored fields from active tab → flat state (for component reads). */
function syncFlatStateFromTab(draft: ChatState, tab: 'think' | 'do') {
  draft.sessionId = draft[tab].sessionId;
  draft.messages = draft[tab].messages;
  draft.isStreaming = draft[tab].isStreaming;
  draft.isCompacting = draft[tab].isCompacting;
  draft.lastStatus = draft[tab].lastStatus;
  draft.tokenUsage = draft[tab].tokenUsage;
  draft.activeTokenUsage = draft[tab].activeTokenUsage;
  draft.pendingInput = draft[tab].pendingInput;       // <-- line 95
  draft.planMode = draft[tab].planMode;
  draft.pendingQuestion = draft[tab].pendingQuestion;
  draft.title = draft[tab].title;
  draft.titleSource = draft[tab].titleSource;
  draft.inputDraft = draft[tab].inputDraft;
}
```

It does **not** call `syncTabStateFromFlat` (which goes the other direction: flat → tab).

